; ==============================================================================
; dotfiles_pasta_inherited_fds.cil
; Stop the audit records pasta writes for descriptors it only inherits.
;
; WHERE THE DENIALS COME FROM. pasta supplies the network for rootless Podman.
; `chezmoi apply` starts it through
; .chezmoiscripts/30-linux/run_after_setup-podman-cluster.sh.tmpl, which calls
; `podman info` and `minikube start --driver=podman` on every apply. The process
; that runs the apply is therefore pasta's ancestor. pasta execs into pasta_t and
; keeps every descriptor that ancestor left open.
;
; When the apply is started from an Electron agent host (Orca IDE), those
; descriptors are the host application's own state: its Chromium caches, leveldb
; stores and dictionaries under ~/.config (config_home_t), and its DRI render
; node /dev/dri/renderD128 (dri_device_t). pasta_t holds no access to either, so
; the kernel writes one AVC record per inherited descriptor. Two pasta processes
; start per apply, which is about 54 records each time.
;
; WHY dontaudit AND NOT allow. pasta never reads or writes these descriptors. It
; has no use for the caller's browser state or GPU node. A dontaudit rule stops
; the audit record and grants nothing, so an access pasta genuinely needs still
; fails and is still logged. An allow rule would hand the container network
; helper the caller's private configuration tree, which is a real widening of the
; sandbox for no gain.
;
; WHY THE PERMISSION SETS CARRY NO `open`. Every denial here is against an
; already-open descriptor. pasta never opens these paths itself, so an `open`
; permission would describe an access that does not occur.
;
; SCOPE. This module suppresses noise only. It is not a protection boundary, and
; it declares no type of its own, so nothing here labels a file or changes what
; any domain may do.
;
; WHY THE RULES SIT IN AN `optional` BLOCK. pasta_t is not part of the base
; Fedora policy. It arrives with passt-selinux, which this repository installs in
; phase 30-components, while this module installs in phase 00. On a host that
; does not have that package yet, an unwrapped reference would fail to resolve at
; `semodule -i` time, and the installer runs under `set -euo pipefail` at the
; first script of the apply — so the apply would abort before the phase that
; supplies the type could ever run, on every subsequent attempt. An `optional`
; block is dropped when a symbol in it does not resolve, so the module installs
; cleanly and starts suppressing once passt-selinux is present.
; ==============================================================================

(optional dotfiles_pasta_inherited_fds_opt
  ; Chromium state the Electron caller left open: GPUCache, DawnWebGPUCache,
  ; DawnGraphiteCache, Local Storage leveldb, and the spellcheck dictionaries.
  (dontaudit pasta_t config_home_t (file (read write append)))

  ; The caller's DRI render node, inherited the same way.
  (dontaudit pasta_t dri_device_t (chr_file (read write)))
)
